  "id": "COMPOUND:24082 - PROTEIN:684",
  "verbalization": "Kusulactone appears to have multiple targets that ultimately lead to Diacylglycerol kinase alpha through a series of biochemical pathways. The evidence suggests that Kusulactone interacts with CAMP phosphodiesterase and phosphatidylinositol 5-phosphate 4-kinase type-2 beta, both of which are targets of other compounds, including Chicoric Acid and CID 92854548. These targets are implicated in the regulation of diacylglycerol kinase alpha, a key enzyme in lipid signaling. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism where Kusulactone may modulate the activity of downstream targets, influencing the function of diacylglycerol kinase alpha. The evidence supports a role for Kusulactone in the regulation of lipid metabolism through these interconnected targets, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
